// Regression for issue #350: a self-recursive local `fun`, declared inside
// a `try` block and never called. The `catch (e)` clause binds `e` with a
// SET_LOCAL that used to read-before-write the slot it reuses, to decide
// whether that slot already held a capture cell (isFreshDeclaration's own
// note in jvm_emitter.cpp). That read sits at the very top of the handler,
// so the classic verifier assembling this backend's classes (no
// StackMapTable) saw it as reachable before `f`'s own slot was ever
// written, and rejected the class with "VerifyError: Register N contains
// wrong type" -- even though `f` is never actually called.

try {
    fun f() { return f(); }
    print "declared";
} catch (e) { print "no"; }

// CHECK: declared
